    <bpmn:process id="W_W4980" name="W4980. Pickup-Channel Fraud, Identity &amp; Release-Integrity Controls" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Suspicious pickup; identity/ownership mismatch; fraud alert
Frequency: Event-driven × 200 stores
Volume: ~100–300 pickup-fraud attempts/at-risk events per year across 200 stores
Owner: LP (VS-23) / Loading-Zone Supervisor / Fraud (VS-125)
Participants: LP (VS-23), Counter Staff (W4962), Fraud (VS-125), CX (VS-13), Finance (VS-17)
Source: workflow W4980 — Pickup-Channel Fraud, Identity &amp; Release-Integrity Controls</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4980_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4980_Lane1" name="Counter Staff">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4980_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4980_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4980_Lane2" name="LP">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4980_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4980_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4980_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4980_Start4" name="Suspicious pickup; identity/ownership mismatch; fraud alert">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4980_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4980_Task5" name="Verify identity &amp; ownership at release: ID/order verification (W4962) to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Verify identity &amp; ownership at release: ID/order verification (W4962) to prevent wrong-party release, flagged-orders review (paid status, chargeback risk, fraud-flag links VS-125), and high-value release controls (VS-23)
Responsible (R): Counter Staff / LP
Accountable (A): Loading-Zone Supervisor
Duration: Per pickup</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4980_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4980_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4980_Task6" name="Detect pickup-channel fraud: patterns (duplicate-pickup, identity fraud…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Detect pickup-channel fraud: patterns (duplicate-pickup, identity fraud, collusion, refund-then-pickup, BOPIS-fraud), monitor via the fraud program (VS-125), and flag risky pickups for hold/verification
Responsible (R): LP / Fraud / Analytics
Accountable (A): LP Lead
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4980_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4980_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4980_Task7" name="Investigate &amp; recover: investigate confirmed fraud, recover goods/loss…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Investigate &amp; recover: investigate confirmed fraud, recover goods/loss, escalate to law-enforcement/Legal (VS-100) where material, and feed the fraud program (VS-125) and analytics
Responsible (R): LP / Fraud / Legal / Finance
Accountable (A): LP Lead
Duration: Event-driven</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4980_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4980_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4980_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4980_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4980_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-97 (ensure will-call release integrity &amp; loading safety.) | - CTL-745: ID/order verified; flagged orders reviewed; fraud monitored (VS-125); high-value LP-controlled
Owner: LP (VS-23) / Loading-Zone Supervisor / Fraud (VS-125)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
