    <bpmn:process id="W_W4984" name="W4984. Customer Pickup Channel Data Privacy, Consent &amp; Records Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer data captured (ID, contact, vehicle); privacy review; DSAR
Frequency: Continuous + periodic review
Volume: ~400,000–600,000 pickup customer records across 200 stores (rolling 24 months)
Owner: DPO/Privacy (VS-91) / Customer Pickup Program Manager
Participants: Privacy/DPO (VS-91), Store Ops (VS-07), CX (VS-13), IT (VS-27), Legal (VS-100)
Source: workflow W4984 — Customer Pickup Channel Data Privacy, Consent &amp; Records Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4984_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4984_Lane1" name="DPO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4984_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4984_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4984_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4984_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4984_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4984_Start3" name="Customer data captured (ID, contact, vehicle); privacy review; DSAR">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4984_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4984_Task4" name="Govern pickup customer data per RA 10173: minimize data captured at pickup (ID…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Govern pickup customer data per RA 10173: minimize data captured at pickup (ID verification, contact for notification, vehicle — links VS-91), consent for marketing/contact, purpose limitation (pickup fulfillment only), and retention limits
Responsible (R): DPO / Program Manager / IT / Legal
Accountable (A): DPO
Duration: Per review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4984_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4984_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4984_Task5" name="Manage the data lifecycle &amp; DSAR: capture/store/secure pickup records, handle…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Manage the data lifecycle &amp; DSAR: capture/store/secure pickup records, handle data-subject requests (access/correction/deletion links VS-91 W271), and dispose per the retention schedule (links VS-88)
Responsible (R): DPO / IT / CX
Accountable (A): DPO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4984_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4984_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4984_Task6" name="Audit &amp; assure: periodic privacy audit of the pickup channel (links VS-91)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Audit &amp; assure: periodic privacy audit of the pickup channel (links VS-91), breach response readiness (VS-91), and training of counter/loading staff on data minimization
Responsible (R): DPO / Internal Audit (VS-21) / Training
Accountable (A): DPO
Duration: Periodic</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4984_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4984_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4984_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4984_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4984_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-745 (ensure controlled execution — Pickup Experience, Exceptions, Chargeback &amp; Analytics (PA-171.3).) | - CTL-745: data minimized &amp; consented; purpose-limited; retention enforced; DSAR handled; audited (VS-91)
Owner: DPO/Privacy (VS-91) / Customer Pickup Program Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
